            <ArticleTitle>Management of insomnia in hospitalized patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>398-404</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In hospitalized patients, the commonest causes of acute insomnia are the effects of illness, environmental sleep disruption, medication, anxiety, and depression. Treatment should correct underlying medical disorders; reduce environmental sleep disruptions; and lower anxiety with psychological interventions, sedative or hypnotic medication, and relaxation training. Special clinical problems include chronic pain, delirium, and insomnia in the elderly.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
